Barney Teletubbies Bluey of all the  children's TV mascots one of the most  famous has to be Thomas the Tank Engine  but what if Thomas had a more Sinister  side that's what developer 2 Star game  sets out to explore in his upcoming game  choo choo Charles from the island to the  train cult to Charles himself here's  everything to know about choo choo  Charles  choo choo Charles transports you to an  unnamed Island in which your only means  of transportation is a small  single-person train as you navigate the  island on the tracks sometimes debris  blocks your path or you may have to  change the track depending on which  direction you want to go be warned  however that when you leave your Little  Engine That Could the arachnid  locomotive Charles is always stalking  the island and you never know when he  might pop up when you are out of the  train be sure not to wander away too far  from the locomotive or else Charles will  find you and chase you down he also  chases you when you're in the train just  to be clear  in addition to leaving a train to clear  your path you can exit your ride to  scavenge for upgrades and talk to the  settlers of the island for Missions one  of the main ways to find upgradeable  scraps or Collectibles for your train is  to loot the areas taken over by the  Charles worshiping cult that lives on  the island although you do not have any  weapons on your person to take out the  cultists you can lure them back to your  train and use the same weapons that you  use against Charles to fend them off  even using the train itself to flatten  them speaking of weapons let's talk  about the Arsenal and these are all  named by the community which I think is  pretty neat the derailleur that's your  default machine gun with low damage but  medium range and medium fire rate the  bug spray a standard flamethrower with  low damage the lowest range but a  massive fire rate the Boomer a rocket  launcher with massive damage but low  range and fire rate and Bob the long  range option with medium damage but high  range and decent fire rate Combat with  Charles has you switching weapons  constantly depending on the damage you  want to deal and how much space you want  to make between Charles and your train  remember those scraps be sure to hold on  to those because they can help you heal  your train during the heat of battle  Charles only takes a little damage  during each encounter before he Retreats  back to stalking the island so be  diligent about how you upgrade and  outfit your train  two star games has detailed that he has  about three main story missions to be  able to upgrade the guns and train to  take down Charles there are some side  missions that involve collecting orbs  from the cultists that will summon  Charles for the final showdown two star  games has said that if you're rushing  through you can complete the game in  about two hours but it will take most  players about three to four hours to  complete  outside of his explanation that the  cultists are around the island for the  sole purpose of gathering offerings and  sacrifices to feed Charles there isn't  much in the way of a story two star  games has stated that the game starts in  one place and ends in one place meaning  the opening and ending are always the  same but how you get there could change  depending on how you play in his  development update videos two star games  does hint a lot at the potential story  that hasn't been released yet namely why  Charles and the island exist in the  first place I guess we'll have to wait  to launch to find out  choo choo Charles is being developed by  two star games which consists of one  person Gavin Eisen bites he has been  making the game for just over a year and  has been documenting his journey  primarily on Tick Tock but also YouTube  and Twitter I'll tag his info in the  description so you can check it out too  although choo choo Charles is his most  recent game two star games got their  start with my beautiful paper smile a  handcrafted horror game in the style of  a demonic Sketchbook it's available to  play right now on Steam as of the  published date of this video choo choo  Charles is only available on Steam  although Gavin has said that he would  love to Port it to consoles at some  point in the next year Gavin also notes  that he will not be moving on to other  projects and supporting the game in the  months after release even though there  will be no dedicated multiplayer mode  choo choo Charles is available now to  wishlist on Steam and will cost 19.99 US  dollars with the price localized for  every region the game releases on  December 9th  choo choo Charles is the latest in the  growing trend of childhood mascots  turned demonic Killers remember that  Winnie the Pooh horror movie that comes  out next year although I don't know how  I feel about a demonic version of one of  my favorite childhood shows I am excited  to face off against Charles and his  merry band of cultists I'll link all of  Gavin's socials in the description catch  me on Twitter at Stewie review and  thanks for watching
 

